// V1 RAW records are followed by raw_timing_count uint16_t durations. V2
// extended RAW records keep this fixed-size record, store their uint32_t
// timing count in parsed_key, and are followed by uint32_t durations. Keeping
// the record layout stable lets the repository read existing V1 remotes while
// large catalog waveforms remain streamed on SD rather than occupying RAM.
// Frequency and radio parameters are stored directly so future preset-table
// changes cannot alter the meaning of an already-saved waveform.
